animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we'll get some interesting Wan Kuei stuff in the story teller's vault.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the hope, and it might happen with V5 open to the Vault now. But hopefully it will be handled with more skill and sensitivity in the future.<br /> <br /> Edit: Back to the subject, how playable is L.A. by now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T12:33:43-07:00","id":1466044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466042#post1466042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is the hope, and it might happen with V5 open to the Vault now. But hopefully it will be handled with more skill and sensitivity in the future.<br /> <br /> Edit: Back to the subject, how playable is L.A. by now?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I'm hoping for. Love the core idea of them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T14:01:44-07:00","id":1466049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466021#post1466021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I disagree but this is the wrong forum to discuss that. Each gameline has its own central premise and while it's nice to think the mages are just full of hubris, I don't think it's the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>You' can disagree all you like, but your position isn't supported by the game itself. Cosmological constants that exist independent of consensus are a thing in Mage. That's just how it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T14:22:47-07:00","id":1466051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1465987#post1465987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Christian God is an evil Wyrm corrupted weaver spirit called the Patriarch according to the Black Furies. A pagan Mother Goddess is the supreme deity.<br /> <br /> In Mage, God does not exist unless humans imagined him up because everything is due to what you believe being true.<br /> <br /> Changelings state the Tuatha De Daanan and Formori are the supreme deities of the world because they are the original incarnations of dream and nightmare.<br /> <br /> Wraith explicitly makes it clear there is no Heaven for the majority of beings, just the Far Shores.<br /> <br /> And YEC isn't even true in DEMON: THE FALLEN. Demons routinely discuss events happening millions and billions of years ago. Not that the majority of Abrahamic faiths believe in YEC either but that's separate.<br /> <br /> We also know its wrong in other lines because the Mokole remember back millions of years.<br /> <br /> These are not small details.</div> </div> </div> </div>The official stance on the &quot;Abrahamic&quot; faith in the books is complex, but is there.<br /> <br /> I think the first thing to do is go down with this &quot;Abrahamic&quot;. No matter what some people pretend to mean, we're talking Christianity. As much as there is a relationship between Christianity and other Abrahamic faiths, most of the themes and myths we're talking are Christian.<br /> <br /> Now, the game lines were ever cautious in not making the Christian faith as the only possible explanation for things. But they always kept it close by all the same.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is the line that more promptly refuses the Christian mythology, but let's not read more than it says. The Garou have several, inconsistent, interpretations about the world, and the Umbra is a complex place. There we can find many entities that are born from the concept of the Christian God without it meaning that this god <b>is</b> any of those entities. So it never really contradicted Christianity but in the demonstrably fallible beliefs of the Garou.<br /> <br /> Mage really doesn't work like that. The books do define that an underlying reality does exist below the Consensus, and that the Consensus can only go so far about this. Although little is known of this underlying reality, it may include an omnipotent, Magick and Consensus-Immune God. Indeed, it is the belief of many important Traditional Paradigms.<br /> <br /> Changelings don't think the Tuatha and Fomorians are the supreme deities. They believe they are the Primal Kithain. Big difference, as the Changelings don't actually consider in this the origins of the world, or even of the Dreaming, just of their species. They do assume there was a world and a Dreaming before the Tuatha, and probably before the Fomorians.<br /> <br /> Heaven isn't as directly important as people think. Heaven and Hell as we understand them are medieval constructs. Also, Wraith doesn't negate them either, as the Wraiths also have a mysterious &quot;after&quot; they suspect much but know little about.<br /> <br /> Demon may not follow YEC, or even actually need the Christian bible to be true to begin with, no matter how it seems at first glance. But it just can't pretend to hide the iconography and what will be the presumed truth if it must come out.<br /> <br /> Remember also that you can be Christian-based even when you try to avoid it. Witchcraft is an example of an absolutely Christian theme, as it didn't came from pagan religions, but from Christian prejudices and misconceptions about some practices (not all of them religious, even).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T14:41:48-07:00","id":1466053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466051#post1466051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The official stance on the &quot;Abrahamic&quot; faith in the books is complex, but is there.<br /> <br /> I think the first thing to do is go down with this &quot;Abrahamic&quot;. No matter what some people pretend to mean, we're talking Christianity. As much as there is a relationship between Christianity and other Abrahamic faiths, most of the themes and myths we're talking are Christian.<br /> <br /> Now, the game lines were ever cautious in not making the Christian faith as the only possible explanation for things. But they always kept it close by all the same.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is the line that more promptly refuses the Christian mythology, but let's not read more than it says. The Garou have several, inconsistent, interpretations about the world, and the Umbra is a complex place. There we can find many entities that are born from the concept of the Christian God without it meaning that this god <b>is</b> any of those entities. So it never really contradicted Christianity but in the demonstrably fallible beliefs of the Garou.<br /> <br /> Mage really doesn't work like that. The books do define that an underlying reality does exist below the Consensus, and that the Consensus can only go so far about this. Although little is known of this underlying reality, it may include an omnipotent, Magick and Consensus-Immune God. Indeed, it is the belief of many important Traditional Paradigms.<br /> <br /> Changelings don't think the Tuatha and Fomorians are the supreme deities. They believe they are the Primal Kithain. Big difference, as the Changelings don't actually consider in this the origins of the world, or even of the Dreaming, just of their species. They do assume there was a world and a Dreaming before the Tuatha, and probably before the Fomorians.<br /> <br /> Heaven isn't as directly important as people think. Heaven and Hell as we understand them are medieval constructs. Also, Wraith doesn't negate them either, as the Wraiths also have a mysterious &quot;after&quot; they suspect much but know little about.<br /> <br /> Demon may not follow YEC, or even actually need the Christian bible to be true to begin with, no matter how it seems at first glance. But it just can't pretend to hide the iconography and what will be the presumed truth if it must come out.<br /> <br /> Remember also that you can be Christian-based even when you try to avoid it. Witchcraft is an example of an absolutely Christian theme, as it didn't came from pagan religions, but from Christian prejudices and misconceptions about some practices (not all of them religious, even).</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, the idea of not precluding a Christian God is still far and above from endorsing one. Mind you, the fact is that Vampire: The Masquerade's take on Hell, Sin, God, and Demons is also something that has a healthy amount of skepticism to the point of being maltheistic as well. The elements of Christianity used in the book are about as accurate as in Hellblazer and that book was deeply hostile to the concept of traditional Abrhamic religion.<br /> <br /> And I mentioned the Patriarch because the books are about as clear as they can that in Werewolfdom, monotheistic Western religion is something they are the enemy of and the God of it is someone the werewolves loathe. Mind you, the Get also loathe Odin so there's that to.<br /> <br /> But I disagree that it is Christianity entirety as one of the things people tend to act like in, say, Africa was that it wasn't 80% Muslim and likely to believe in Caine as much as any other vampire. It was also another reason the Kuei-Jin were problematic because it acted like the Cainite myth wouldn't be possible in Asia at all when, again, the Muslim portions of the setting would be inclined to view Caine as the Dark Father.<br /> <br /> Either way, the primary issue is that Abrahamic religion is not being forwarded as the Grand Unifying Cosmology of all the gamelines. It is, yes, pretty central to V:TM and D:TF but I feel like the whole point of the World of Darkness is its a Religious Kitchen Sink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T15:57:29-07:00","id":1466057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466053#post1466053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, the primary issue is that Abrahamic religion is not being forwarded as the Grand Unifying Cosmology of all the gamelines. It is, yes, pretty central to V:TM and D:TF but I feel like the whole point of the World of Darkness is its a Religious Kitchen Sink.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some points:<br /> <br /> 1- As I already mentioned, hostility to Christianity doesn't equate to denying Christianity. It does equate to resignifying Christianity. From a hostile perspective it is bad, from a foreign perspective it means nothing. <b>That</b> is Christianity from a non-Abrahamic perspective, a big bunch of meaningless legends.<br /> <br /> 2- The Furies also have a camp of <b>nuns</b>. That aside, Garou are animistic, but the question here isn't the IC beliefs, but the OoC cosmology and how many elements it have that endorse or not any given religion, how many alternate religions can be forwarded as option, and how easy. I already said the setting never makes Christianity the only possible explanation, but it is always among the simpler ones.<br /> <br /> By the way, although it is best explored on Hengeyokai, even the beliefs of the Garou are full of holes about the beginning, with Gaia being their great mother but not necessarily the origin of everything and when they forward a myth that can cover the beginning of the universe... it is either Christian or can be easily read as such.<br /> <br /> Now, how much effort do you need to put to take any other religion and make it the ultimate explanation of the universe? Not saying you can't, but is the amount of effort similar?<br /> <br /> 3- Christianity. It is definitely Christianity. It doesn't matter if Cain exist for all the Abrahamic religions, he's there because of Christianity. So much so that elements of the other Abrahamic religions, big and small, aren't there unless they also exist in Christianity, while there are Christian themes in the setting that don't exist in the other Abrahamic religions.<br /> <br /> 4- I don't get what you want to say with the part on the myth of Caine in Asia. Can you elaborate?<br /> <br /> 5- The WoD is far from a religious kitchen sink. There is a stark contrast on how much attention and well developed are different religions involved. It isn't half bad given its history, but it is marked by its history. The Umbrae may be fantastic cosmologies, but they're game cosmologies. Every time things get to describe religion, Christianity have a stronger foothold in the setting, followed by puerile renditions of few others.<br /> <br /> Some got completely butchered, as actual polytheism was unceremoniously shoved inside animism-like. Either there is no god or there is The God. It makes sense, as the original authors have little to no knowledge outside Christianity, and later authors had less and less space to add something of significance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T16:10:41-07:00","id":1466059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466057#post1466057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some points:<br /> <br /> 1- As I already mentioned, hostility to Christianity doesn't equate to denying Christianity. It does equate to resignifying Christianity. From a hostile perspective it is bad, from a foreign perspective it means nothing. <b>That</b> is Christianity from a non-Abrahamic perspective, a big bunch of meaningless legends.<br /> <br /> 2- The Furies also have a camp of <b>nuns</b>. That aside, Garou are animistic, but the question here isn't the IC beliefs, but the OoC cosmology and how many elements it have that endorse or not any given religion, how many alternate religions can be forwarded as option, and how easy. I already said the setting never makes Christianity the only possible explanation, but it is always among the simpler ones.<br /> <br /> By the way, although it is best explored on Hengeyokai, even the beliefs of the Garou are full of holes about the beginning, with Gaia being their great mother but not necessarily the origin of everything and when they forward a myth that can cover the beginning of the universe... it is either Christian or can be easily read as such.<br /> <br /> Now, how much effort do you need to put to take any other religion and make it the ultimate explanation of the universe? Not saying you can't, but is the amount of effort similar?<br /> <br /> 3- Christianity. It is definitely Christianity. It doesn't matter if Cain exist for all the Abrahamic religions, he's there because of Christianity. So much so that elements of the other Abrahamic religions, big and small, aren't there unless they also exist in Christianity, while there are Christian themes in the setting that don't exist in the other Abrahamic religions.<br /> <br /> 4- I don't get what you want to say with the part on the myth of Caine in Asia. Can you elaborate?<br /> <br /> 5- The WoD is far from a religious kitchen sink. There is a stark contrast on how much attention and well developed are different religions involved. It isn't half bad given its history, but it is marked by its history. The Umbrae may be fantastic cosmologies, but they're game cosmologies. Every time things get to describe religion, Christianity have a stronger foothold in the setting, followed by puerile renditions of few others.<br /> <br /> Some got completely butchered, as actual polytheism was unceremoniously shoved inside animism-like. Either there is no god or there is The God. It makes sense, as the original authors have little to no knowledge outside Christianity, and later authors had less and less space to add something of significance.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Does that mean anything in a game that everyone considers fictional?<br /> <br /> 2a. Yes, the nuns worship Gaia.<br /> <br /> 2b. I feel that is an incredible stretch as the Garou DO have a Creation Myth and that is everything was created by the WEAVER. They are the Creator being.<br /> <br /> 3. I feel like this <b>DRAMATICALLY</b> overstates the role of Caine in Christianity where he is a almost nonexistent figure, including in European Mythology.<br /> <br /> 4. Bluntly, the treatment of all of Asia as falling under the auspices of the Kuei Jin was highly orientalist as it demeaned everything to being a bastarded Chinese mythology and ignoring the Caine myth among Islamic societies was really racist. There's a billion Muslims in Asia.<br /> <br /> 5. It has a blasphemous anti-Christianity that has a lot of attention. Which is a bizarre take to forward on.<br /> <br /> But this doesn't seem like it discusses LA by Night much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T16:25:55-07:00","id":1466060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466059#post1466059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Does that mean anything in a game that everyone considers fictional?<br /> <br /> 2a. Yes, the nuns worship Gaia.<br /> <br /> 2b. I feel that is an incredible stretch as the Garou DO have a Creation Myth and that is everything was created by the WEAVER. They are the Creator being.<br /> <br /> 3. I feel like this <b>DRAMATICALLY</b> overstates the role of Caine in Christianity where he is a almost nonexistent figure, including in European Mythology.<br /> <br /> 4. Bluntly, the treatment of all of Asia as falling under the auspices of the Kuei Jin was highly orientalist as it demeaned everything to being a bastarded Chinese mythology and ignoring the Caine myth among Islamic societies was really racist. There's a billion Muslims in Asia.<br /> <br /> 5. It has a blasphemous anti-Christianity that has a lot of attention. Which is a bizarre take to forward on.<br /> <br /> But this doesn't seem like it discusses LA by Night much.</div> </div> </div> </div>1- If it didn't meant there would be no players complaining. Those complaints exist because those elements matter to the players, and those players cover all those other religions;<br /> <br /> 2a- Yet they were nuns, not nun-like or infiltrated, but actual nuns, so the Church at least didn't offended them nearly as much, that's my point;<br /> <br /> 2b- No, their creation myth includes the Wyld creating stuff and the Weaver solidifying forms. But the myth doesn't account for the origin of the first spirits, and the three weren't the first ones, some other spirits preceded them;<br /> <br /> 3- It is not only about Cain. Cain, indeed, isn't important (by the way, Cain. Caine with an &quot;e&quot; is the in-game version);<br /> <br /> 4- They didn't ignore the Caine myth among Muslims, the Muslims are Kindred. Most of the Ashirra is in Asia, and they have elements as far as China, that is indeed the main spread of Islam in Asia. The rest is, indeed, quite correct;<br /> <br /> 5- For the non-Christian players it may, sometimes, be more important to recognize that their religions exist than to chose between bashing or praising Christianity.<br /> <br /> 6- You are right, but this is a sore point to me as I'm one of those players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T16:40:50-07:00","id":1466061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466060#post1466060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- If it didn't meant there would be no players complaining. Those complaints exist because those elements matter to the players, and those players cover all those other religions;<br /> <br /> 2a- Yet they were nuns, not nun-like or infiltrated, but actual nuns, so the Church at least didn't offended them nearly as much, that's my point;<br /> <br /> 2b- No, their creation myth includes the Wyld creating stuff and the Weaver solidifying forms. But the myth doesn't account for the origin of the first spirits, and the three weren't the first ones, some other spirits preceded them;<br /> <br /> 3- It is not only about Cain. Cain, indeed, isn't important (by the way, Cain. Caine with an &quot;e&quot; is the in-game version);<br /> <br /> 4- They didn't ignore the Caine myth among Muslims, the Muslims are Kindred. Most of the Ashirra is in Asia, and they have elements as far as China, that is indeed the main spread of Islam in Asia. The rest is, indeed, quite correct;<br /> <br /> 5- For the non-Christian players it may, sometimes, be more important to recognize that their religions exist than to chose between bashing or praising Christianity.<br /> <br /> 6- You are right, but this is a sore point to me as I'm one of those players.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. What is the complaint? That the premise is vampirism is Judeo-Christian based in its mythology?<br /> <br /> 2a . Ummm, that's not how it works. The Followers of Set have some of their members as Catholic Priests but the fact they worship Set means that they are NOT actual Christian priests. By being Gaian worshiping nuns, they are by definition infilitrators as they worship Gaia instead of the Patriarch/God.<br /> <br /> 2b. The Triat either sprang from the Wyld or was always there. No higher spirit exists than them in Garou mythology.<br /> <br /> 3. It is a reminder that applying &quot;Christian&quot; as a label is weird given it's an Old Testament Creation myth.<br /> <br /> 4. Alright.<br /> <br /> 5. Yes and I support alternate mythologies but the game should also stick with its existing mythology because a large part of the social satire is based on subverting Christian mythology.<br /> <br /> 6. What would your solution be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T17:38:23-07:00","id":1466067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466053#post1466053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I mentioned the Patriarch because the books are about as clear as they can that in Werewolfdom, monotheistic Western religion is something they are the enemy of and the God of it is someone the werewolves loathe. Mind you, the Get also loathe Odin so there's that to.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it just shows that whoever came up with the Patriarch knows shit-all about Christianity as a Christian would take one look at the Werewolf cosmology and say \u201cwe worship the First Cause and Unmoved Mover\u201d i.e. whatever force created Gaia/the Cosmos (or Gaia itself depending on your particular interpretation and female for Gaia is no more accurate than male is for the Christian God\u2026 it\u2019s a label applied by humans to try and wrap their head around a supreme creator who is further beyond us that we are beyond the bacteria in our guts).<br /> <br /> The Patriarch reads like something developed by someone who never looked beyond some typical anti-Christian propaganda akin to trusting a white supremacist for accurate information about cultures in Africa. Frankly, if that approach were being applied to any other religion, the author would have been driven out of society for their cultural insensitivity.<br /> <br /> ETA: to sum it up, any created entity would be immediately classified as a false god (about which the Bible warns) by any Christian this could be proven to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 10-31-2021, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T17:52:15-07:00","id":1466072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466067#post1466067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it just shows that whoever came up with the Patriarch knows shit-all about Christianity as a Christian would take one look at the Werewolf cosmology and say \u201cwe worship the First Cause and Unmoved Mover\u201d i.e. whatever force created Gaia/the Cosmos (or Gaia itself depending on your particular interpretation and female for Gaia is no more accurate than male is for the Christian God\u2026 it\u2019s a label applied by humans to try and wrap their head around a supreme creator who is further beyond us that we are beyond the bacteria in our guts).<br /> <br /> The Patriarch reads like something developed by someone who never looked beyond some typical anti-Christian propaganda akin to trusting a white supremacist for accurate information about cultures in Africa. Frankly, if that approach were being applied to any other religion, the author would have been driven out of society for their cultural insensitivity.<br /> <br /> ETA: to sum it up, any created entity would be immediately classified as a false god (about which the Bible warns) by any Christian this could be proven to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have missed the point. Of course it's anti-Christian propaganda. They're animist pagans. There's no attempt at respect in Werewolf: The Apocalypse's 1st Edition tribe books. It is quite the opposite and meant to be offensive and insulting. In the tribe book, the Patriarch is a direct and explicit slam on Abrahamic religion both in and out of universe.<br /> <br /> Because Christianity is not true in the setting.<br /> <br /> As a direct contrast to Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> This is me speaking as a liberal Christian in RL. It's like suggesting there's a god above the Force in Star Wars. It's against the internal setting's logic.<br /> <br /> Obviously individual STs can decide what is true in their settings. Also, the fact is that they'll have to decide which setting is &quot;right&quot; if there's a combined WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-31-2021, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T20:35:53-07:00","id":1466085,"title":"","content":"Whoever's right or wrong, it's going to be millennia of blood in Asia, because the vampires can never avoid being tainted in even a polite appearance. Say goodbye to courts meeting peacefully between vampires and werebeasts; the former are likely to be on the shit list of the latter, with nothing to stop naked conflict between the two. At best, it's akin to where the Garou Nation is with the Cam, but if the Garou Nation had easy access to Gifts and rites that invoke the power of the sun.<br /> <br /> And if the Sabbat is in control, the Beast Courts are highly unlikely to hold back in any way. Attack caern, get stomped on by Gozilla-sized Middle Dragon. Then, of course, the kin have to pitch in to fill the footprints that they leave behind...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T20:38:00-07:00","id":1466086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466085#post1466085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoever's right or wrong, it's going to be millennia of blood in Asia, because the vampires can never avoid being tainted in even a polite appearance. Say goodbye to courts meeting peacefully between vampires and werebeasts; the former are likely to be on the shit list of the latter, with nothing to stop naked conflict between the two. At best, it's akin to where the Garou Nation is with the Cam, but if the Garou Nation had easy access to Gifts and rites that invoke the power of the sun.<br /> <br /> And if the Sabbat is in control, the Beast Courts are highly unlikely to hold back in any way. Attack caern, get stomped on by Gozilla-sized Middle Dragon. Then, of course, the kin have to pitch in to fill the footprints that they leave behind...</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I love the Gifts and Rites that can invoke the sun, they basically work like fire anyway. Its not quite the OP power that it seems.<br /> <br /> My opinion is that the Beast Courts fully intend to exterminate the vampires around them....once they get done dealing with the Werewolves, Demons, and other threats. Just like Garou and Western vampires. Mind you, I now want to know if the Kuei-Jin are gone does this mean that the Chinese Salubri are fine? I assume without the Wan Kuei hating Saulot that they'd do fine there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T20:54:23-07:00","id":1466088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466072#post1466072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you have missed the point. Of course it's anti-Christian propaganda. They're animist pagans. There's no attempt at respect in Werewolf: The Apocalypse's 1st Edition tribe books. It is quite the opposite and meant to be offensive and insulting. In the tribe book, the Patriarch is a direct and explicit slam on Abrahamic religion both in and out of universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I get the point, the writer was either too ignorant or spiteful to get that their Patriarch figure would be utterly rejected by any real Christian in or out of universe as a false god. It is literally the opposite of actual Christian doctrine and if they pulled the same stunt on, say, Native American religion, would no longer be employed.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s Wendigo level misinterpretation in that it\u2019s saying Christians literally worship what their religion calls The Devil (a false god who is not the Creator of All, but pretends to be). If calling one of the Garou tribes the Wendigo is wrong, then so is presenting The Patriarch as the Christian God unless you\u2019re an abject hypocrite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is me speaking as a liberal Christian in RL. It's like suggesting there's a god above the Force in Star Wars. </div> </div> </div> Objectively speaking, unless the Force created the Star Wars universe*, there must be something analogous to the Christian understanding of God in it. Ultimately if you follow the chain of causality back there must be a First Cause or there can be no effects or subsequent causes that follow.<br /> <br /> So, using our present model of the universe, something caused the Big Bang, and if you say it was just a random fluctuation in the quantum vacuum, fine. But what caused there to be the quantum vacuum? Go back as many layers as you want, but sooner or later you hit the First Cause\u2026 and that First Cause is what Christians call God and it so far beyond us in scope that even trying to claim to understand it\u2019s true nature is like a single cell trying to contemplate its existence within not a person, or the planet, but in the entire universe.<br /> <br /> * which, given what we know of The Force is entirely possible, in which case The Force IS what Christians call God and it\u2019s manifestations within living beings are akin to the Holy Spirit. The only element arguing against that is the claim that life creates The Force\u2026 in which case, see above because something created the life and the universe and everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T20:56:35-07:00","id":1466089,"title":"","content":"To get back to LA by Night, I think the biggest thing this series did was help solidify &quot;How to play V5&quot; in the minds of gamers and give audienecs who might have not been otherwise receptive to the Edition a chance to see how you're supposed to do it.<br /> <br /> Some things I think it did very well:<br /> <br /> <u>Positives</u><br /> <br /> * <b>The Anarchs are not morons:</b> We have a Ventrue, Toreador, and Nosferatu Anarch party in addition to the usual Brujah. Yes, there's infighting among the baronies but they're generally all allied under Baron Isaac Abrams against external threats.<br /> <br /> * <b>The Anarch hypocrisy is subtle not overt</b>: What do you call a Baron that is significantly more powerful than all the other Barons and can dictate the territory of other Barons? The Barons who all support him as their leader? Yes, Isaac Abrams is PRINCE of LA. He's also why LA is no longer a clusterfuck. Annabelle is the only die-hard true believer and is shown to be a mouthpiece they use for propaganda purposes.<br /> <br /> * <b>The Second Inquisition is not shown to be all powerful</b>: It is dangerous but gets befuddled and thrown about numerous times. Like the time they try to ally with a local vampire against the others, try (and fail) to keep Fiona, and other business. It still inflicts some pretty heavy casualties on the undead.<br /> <br /> * <b>Camarilla hypocrisy is shown</b>: Fiorenza is aiding Victor Temple in his rise to power even though she's a Camarilla oligarch. Why? Because controlling him gives her influence in the Anarchs and she has favors she can call upon just the same as the reverse.<br /> <br /> * <b>The Camarilla's weaknesses are also shown</b>: The Camarilla dismisses any of Victor's ideas about allying against the Second Inquisition, throws its weight around, and refuses to acknowlege the Anarchs as anything other than errant children. It's also technologically inept.<br /> <br /> * <b>The past is still there</b>: References to MacNeil, Bloodlines, Zellios, Beckett, and so much else help ground LA by Night in the present. Hell, we even have Francois Villon, Lucita, and Karsh show up.<br /> <br /> Less so:<br /> <br /> <u>Weaknesses</u><br /> <br /> * <b>Frenzies</b>: I feel like we only had one the entire season and that was Victor biting a guy. Maybe also Nelli eating one of Victor's people. I feel like we should have had more. Annabelle should have certainly had some.<br /> <br /> * <b>Dropped Plotlines</b>: Delilah diablerizing Tremere in order to become more powerful and cease being a Thin Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T01:51:52-07:00","id":1466099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466067#post1466067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it just shows that whoever came up with the Patriarch knows shit-all about Christianity as a Christian would take one look at the Werewolf cosmology and say \u201cwe worship the First Cause and Unmoved Mover\u201d i.e. whatever force created Gaia/the Cosmos (or Gaia itself depending on your particular interpretation and female for Gaia is no more accurate than male is for the Christian God\u2026 it\u2019s a label applied by humans to try and wrap their head around a supreme creator who is further beyond us that we are beyond the bacteria in our guts).<br /> <br /> The Patriarch reads like something developed by someone who never looked beyond some typical anti-Christian propaganda akin to trusting a white supremacist for accurate information about cultures in Africa. Frankly, if that approach were being applied to any other religion, the author would have been driven out of society for their cultural insensitivity.<br /> <br /> ETA: to sum it up, any created entity would be immediately classified as a false god (about which the Bible warns) by any Christian this could be proven to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, as someone whose had a lot of experience with certain evangelical apocalyptic cults that come under the umbrella of Christianity the God I was exposed to on a constant basis was a pretty damn good match for the Patriach....especially the way it was used by the men in the organisations to dominate, abuse and control women, children and LGBTQ folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T01:55:46-07:00","id":1466100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466086#post1466086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as I love the Gifts and Rites that can invoke the sun, they basically work like fire anyway. Its not quite the OP power that it seems.<br /> <br /> My opinion is that the Beast Courts fully intend to exterminate the vampires around them....once they get done dealing with the Werewolves, Demons, and other threats. Just like Garou and Western vampires. Mind you, I now want to know if the Kuei-Jin are gone does this mean that the Chinese Salubri are fine? I assume without the Wan Kuei hating Saulot that they'd do fine there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lets face it any books on Asia/Oceania/Africa/Central America/South America etc. for V5 are going to be Storytellers Vault books anyway based on current trajectory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T02:27:34-07:00","id":1466101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466100#post1466100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets face it any books on Asia/Oceania/Africa/Central America/South America etc. for V5 are going to be Storytellers Vault books anyway based on current trajectory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'm not so sure. Renegade managed to put out these books pretty fast by comparison. I have the idea if they just told, &quot;Justin, go write this&quot; he'd have it out in a month. I also think OPP is capable of churning out books as well as anyone. They just need to hire the write people. If they wanted to Vampires of the World, they could hire all the enthusiastic V:TM fans of their countries of origin they wanted.<br /> <br /> Outstar did a interview with the head of Brazil's massive V:TM community not too long ago for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T02:31:45-07:00","id":1466102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466101#post1466101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I'm not so sure. Renegade managed to put out these books pretty fast by comparison. I have the idea if they just told, &quot;Justin, go write this&quot; he'd have it out in a month. I also think OPP is capable of churning out books as well as anyone. They just need to hire the write people. If they wanted to Vampires of the World, they could hire all the enthusiastic V:TM fans of their countries of origin they wanted.<br /> <br /> Outstar did a interview with the head of Brazil's massive V:TM community not too long ago for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well...I envy your optimism. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T02:50:38-07:00","id":1466103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466102#post1466102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...I envy your optimism. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, my optimism is driven almost entirely by 3rd party supplements. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T02:53:39-07:00","id":1466104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466099#post1466099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, as someone whose had a lot of experience with certain evangelical apocalyptic cults that come under the umbrella of Christianity the God I was exposed to on a constant basis was a pretty damn good match for the Patriach....especially the way it was used by the men in the organisations to dominate, abuse and control women, children and LGBTQ folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, a non-hostile Garou game would state that the Patriarch is absolutely the classical Demiurge figure: an evil intolerant corruption of religion that takes away from the worship of the &quot;real&quot; God. I had a Children of Gaia youth pastor character (odd concept I know) who just considered Gaia the &quot;true&quot; God. Other Garou found him quite strange but he was a fun concept for a bit.<br /> <br /> They also did roll back the Patriarch's importance in game and made him a Weaver rather than Wyrm spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T03:04:46-07:00","id":1466106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466086#post1466086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as I love the Gifts and Rites that can invoke the sun, they basically work like fire anyway. Its not quite the OP power that it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Aetherial Gifts indicate a much more varied potential, one of which is &quot;living or undead targets roll Stamina difficulty 9 to avoid dying&quot;, and also burns out corruption in survivors. If you want to run things like how the BSDs get hit by it, you could have the vampire roll their Generation dots (also diff 9) and, if they don't succeed, knock them down to where they were when they first got embraced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My opinion is that the Beast Courts fully intend to exterminate the vampires around them....once they get done dealing with the Werewolves, Demons, and other threats. Just like Garou and Western vampires. Mind you, I now want to know if the Kuei-Jin are gone does this mean that the Chinese Salubri are fine? I assume without the Wan Kuei hating Saulot that they'd do fine there. </div> </div> </div>Well, with Yama Kings unlikely to make a return, their dance card is probably open again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T03:27:25-07:00","id":1466107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466106#post1466106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, with Yama Kings unlikely to make a return, their dance card is probably open again...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also not like the Wyrm and all its massive armies of evil aren't going to be in Asia either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mind you, I am now curious if there's a Chinese equivalent to Pentex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T06:37:46-07:00","id":1466119,"title":"","content":"Likes:<br /> I enjoyed the series for showing a different way of playing to the usual D&amp;D type game, and giving me plenty of ideas on things to try. <br /> <br /> The last episode redeemed a lot with some great send offs.<br /> <br /> The very clear indication that the hunters were still out there, and a bit more complicated in their relationships. <br /> <br /> Dislikes:<br /> I wish the Camarilla had hung around and Vannevar had been given a chance to go after the PCs in a non-violent way. After killing a Sheriff or two, a harpy and then refusing to accept the Prince's rule I was always waiting for some sort of retaliation. I also think the setting would be in a more interesting place than it is now. Feels a bit like a Simpsons episode where a lot of stuff has happened but at the end of the day nothing has really changed. <br /> <br /> Overall lots of fun though<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T06:40:25-07:00","id":1466120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brickman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466119#post1466119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likes:<br /> I enjoyed the series for showing a different way of playing to the usual D&amp;D type game, and giving me plenty of ideas on things to try.<br /> <br /> The last episode redeemed a lot with some great send offs.<br /> <br /> The very clear indication that the hunters were still out there, and a bit more complicated in their relationships.<br /> <br /> Dislikes:<br /> I wish the Camarilla had hung around and Vannevar had been given a chance to go after the PCs in a non-violent way. After killing a Sheriff or two, a harpy and then refusing to accept the Prince's rule I was always waiting for some sort of retaliation. I also think the setting would be in a more interesting place than it is now. Feels a bit like a Simpsons episode where a lot of stuff has happened but at the end of the day nothing has really changed.<br /> <br /> Overall lots of fun though</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, plot armor aside, they did go after Jasper in retaliation and only were stopped by Strauss getting access to the Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> They were also totally planning on just straight up murdering Victor in Episode 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T07:03:23-07:00","id":1466126,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Post Deletion reason: Equating fictional satire with RL hate speech in a game about werewolf eco-warriors.<br /> <br /> If you wish to revive the topic in the Werewolf forum, please do so in a marked thread without the RL comparisons.<br /> <br /> Also, agreed that we should definitely move on from this topic.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T08:51:32-07:00","id":1466130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466061#post1466061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What is the complaint? That the premise is vampirism is Judeo-Christian based in its mythology?<br /> <br /> 2a . Ummm, that's not how it works. The Followers of Set have some of their members as Catholic Priests but the fact they worship Set means that they are NOT actual Christian priests. By being Gaian worshiping nuns, they are by definition infilitrators as they worship Gaia instead of the Patriarch/God.<br /> <br /> 2b. The Triat either sprang from the Wyld or was always there. No higher spirit exists than them in Garou mythology.<br /> <br /> 3. It is a reminder that applying &quot;Christian&quot; as a label is weird given it's an Old Testament Creation myth.<br /> <br /> 4. Alright.<br /> <br /> 5. Yes and I support alternate mythologies but the game should also stick with its existing mythology because a large part of the social satire is based on subverting Christian mythology.<br /> <br /> 6. What would your solution be?</div> </div> </div> </div>1- It would be nice if a game based on our world offered better support for non-Christians working their own religions in;<br /> <br /> 2a- The Church and the Christian faith was far more diversified in the Middle Ages, when they operated, and is still quite varied. I'm from a Roman Catholic country and I know how little uniformity it actually have. Gaia is a Heresy at most, possibly not even that;<br /> <br /> 2b- False. The Garou have no unified myth about their origin and many ascribe at least one other spirit as the creator of the Triat. Although there are some that see them as the origin of everything else (in varied orders), this is no absolute in the setting;<br /> <br /> 3- Even the Old Testament isn't exactly equal in every Abrahamic religion, as some entities and events differ due to very different theological understandings;<br /> <br /> 5- As the setting grew, this focus of the satire on Christianity lost a lot of context. For some, not presenting other religions in a strong place render the satire moot, because they interact with Christianity as outsiders. For others it would be nice to have space for other religious satires, as Christianity have no bearing in their lives;<br /> <br /> 6- Make more clear and easy to explore openings for other possibilities instead of framing everything as Christian or Counter-Christian.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466085#post1466085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say goodbye to courts meeting peacefully between vampires and werebeasts;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that Kindred aren't necessarily so tainted but...<br /> <br /> There is no Kuei-Jin anymore. I don't think there are Beast Courts, either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466089#post1466089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To get back to LA by Night, I think the biggest thing this series did was help solidify &quot;How to play V5&quot; in the minds of gamers and give audienecs who might have not been otherwise receptive to the Edition a chance to see how you're supposed to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good, although I got the impression, from you positives, that it also solidifies the <u>subtext</u> that the Anarchs are the protagonist faction and the Camarilla is ultimately stupid. Am I right, or could you elaborate upon?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466099#post1466099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, as someone whose had a lot of experience with certain evangelical apocalyptic cults that come under the umbrella of Christianity the God I was exposed to on a constant basis was a pretty damn good match for the Patriach....especially the way it was used by the men in the organisations to dominate, abuse and control women, children and LGBTQ folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Patriarch is an anthropology construct that makes a lot of sense as a spirit, but some people have a hard time understanding that their religion is an umbrella with that exists outside their own theological views.<br /> <br /> My first wife was worse, to the point of refusing to recognize Kardecist Spiritism as Christianity and almost doing the same to Catholicism. She didn't denounced those things as heresies, mind you, she outright say it is unrelated to Christianity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466100#post1466100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets face it any books on Asia/Oceania/Africa/Central America/South America etc. for V5 are going to be Storytellers Vault books anyway based on current trajectory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I don't share the same level of optimism as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, I do think they'll work most of those i some way.<br /> <br /> But they'll probably avoid Asia, in my opinion, as they have to decide what to do about the Wan-Kuei and the &quot;Middle East&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T09:11:48-07:00","id":1466134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's good, although I got the impression, from you positives, that it also solidifies the <u>subtext</u> that the Anarchs are the protagonist faction and the Camarilla is ultimately stupid. Am I right, or could you elaborate upon?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's notably an Anarch game set in Los Angeles and the Camarilla is by no means stupid. It is by far the most dangerous and capable foe the protagonists face.<br /> <br /> Baron Victor Temple (one of the PCs) makes numerous attempts to ally with the Camarilla against the Inquisition but is not only rebuffed but it is made clear the Camarilla in LA considers the Anarchs (and Thin Bloods in particular) a much bigger threat. Mind you, Victor is wrong about the Thin Bloods as they begin a campaign of murder and diablerie behind his back. They aren't the innocent victims he believes them to be.<br /> <br /> If you want a canonical Camarilla game, SEATTLE BY NIGHT, which is also run by Jason Carl is a good option. The PCs work hard to put the previous Prince back in power and the Anarchs are made to look like idiots. Which is impressive because these are some of the dumbest PCs of all time.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/f2smsDmVfco/maxresdefault.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-01-2021, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T10:20:59-07:00","id":1466146,"title":"","content":"Considering how the Penny Arcade team... approaches... doing campaigns (you touch on it somewhat with the &quot;dumbest pcs of all time&quot; note), where was it noted that Seattle by Night ended up being canon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-01-2021, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T13:02:52-07:00","id":1466156,"title":"","content":"My opinion may be totally discounted since I am not running any V5 games now or in the near future, but - I <i>have</i> watched and mostly enjoyed LAbN for the past couple years. I think they did well mixing old with new, using fan favorites from Bloodlines without having them overshadow the story, and in their portrayal of the Second Inquisition. The protagonists mostly work for me as introductory characters, since they all more-or-less epitomize the archetypes most associated with their clan. The only one I'd ever consider borrowing for use in a game is Victor, as I see him as best illustrating the strengths and weaknesses of ambitious young anarchs striving to change the status quo.<br /> <br /> FWIW in my V20 game, set more-or-less contemporaneously, the Camarilla is in no position to threaten L.A.---they have far more important battles to fight, since I pushed back the fierce Camarilla/Sabbat battles of Baltimore and Atlanta to the late 2010s; nor has the Sabbat lost its principal North American cities in Mexico and Canada. More worrisome perhaps, L.A. is in the process of being consolidated under one &quot;super-gang,&quot; threatening to herald the birth of a new sect if events aren't reversed there. This new group, adapted from the timeline of the Gehenna Novels and BJD, calls itself <i>The MacNeills</i>---a rich irony considering they have come to represent everything MacNeill struggled to keep the Free State from becoming while he lived; but they have no qualm whatsoever at perverting his memory and martyrdom for propaganda purposes (although once their tendrils have been firmly dug into other Free Cities, a name change to <i>The Syndicate</i> is being mooted). [Sidebar - while the Wan-Kuei in my timeline were heavily checked by the events of <i>Bloodlines</i>, the New Mandrinate still exists and holds on to the core of San Francisco, a city where Kindred are forbidden, while their puppet Jochen Van Nuys claims &quot;praxis&quot; over neighboring San Jose]. On the other hand, the assassination of Hardestadt has grown Theo Bell's legend to the point where he could very well take the place of MacNeill and Garcia, if he cared to fight for it. His disciples can be found in every major city of the USA and speak boldly of his deeds and what can be accomplished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T13:55:48-07:00","id":1466164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1465982#post1465982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the impression they won't even mention them to clarify. But his exact words were, &quot;The Kuei Jin are not part of V5 or our vision.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably going to be a nice little earner for whoever homebrews it first on the vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T14:02:27-07:00","id":1466165,"title":"","content":"There are a few interesting possibilities that could arise in the wake of the series<br /> <br /> 1. Therese may consider coming out of hiding now that the Camarilla is gone, although she may be more worried about the SI than Jeanette. If she does, she'll be by far the most senior baron who actually wants to be a baron.<br /> 2. Nelly and the local SI head have &quot;an understanding&quot;. If they get back to picking off kindred and that somehow comes to light, it could look really bad for her and Greg, even though she isn't actually informing them. She might need her &quot;Divine Purity&quot; loresheet advantage again.<br /> 3. There are almost no Camarilla left for the thin-bloods to diablerise. They may continue to threaten full kindred or their solidarity may collapse after so many go from being &quot;one of us&quot; to &quot;one of them&quot;. Do they know what little Delilah thinks of them?<br /> <br /> <br /> How does <i>Seattle by Night</i> fit with VTMB2? I heard that the former is set in Tacoma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T15:34:16-07:00","id":1466181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466164#post1466164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably going to be a nice little earner for whoever homebrews it first on the vault.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the Vault is there for, alternative product for those who want it and produce it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T15:52:30-07:00","id":1466188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466146#post1466146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how the Penny Arcade team... approaches... doing campaigns (you touch on it somewhat with the &quot;dumbest pcs of all time&quot; note), where was it noted that Seattle by Night ended up being canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I was just assuming it because it was Jason Carl STing it but you're correct that it probably isn't since it's on the Penny Arcade site and not the official World of Darkness one. I imagine that Vein Pursuits IS canon, though, because it's on Youtube's World of Darkness channel.<br /> <br /> Even then, I admit Seattle by Night better reflects how my PCs tend to act versus LA by Night.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466165#post1466165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a few interesting possibilities that could arise in the wake of the series<br /> <br /> 1. Therese may consider coming out of hiding now that the Camarilla is gone, although she may be more worried about the SI than Jeanette. If she does, she'll be by far the most senior baron who actually wants to be a baron.<br /> 2. Nelly and the local SI head have &quot;an understanding&quot;. If they get back to picking off kindred and that somehow comes to light, it could look really bad for her and Greg, even though she isn't actually informing them. She might need her &quot;Divine Purity&quot; loresheet advantage again.<br /> 3. There are almost no Camarilla left for the thin-bloods to diablerise. They may continue to threaten full kindred or their solidarity may collapse after so many go from being &quot;one of us&quot; to &quot;one of them&quot;. Do they know what little Delilah thinks of them?<br /> <br /> <br /> How does <i>Seattle by Night</i> fit with VTMB2? I heard that the former is set in Tacoma.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I think the Anarch book established Therese relocates to Las Vegas at some point, so she's likely to remain there. Its possible she just franchised and visited, though.<br /> 2. I think Nelli is outright engaged in treason as vampires would argue it. The irony being that Jasper was entirely right she's &quot;ugly on the inside.&quot; Being a Baron has utterly gone to her head. To be fair, Victor did probably want to take over.<br /> 3. I mean, Delilah is a huge twist and being a Kindred utterly warped her. I really liked that and think Victor will regret not destroying her/handing her over to the Camarilla.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-01-2021, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T16:40:01-07:00","id":1466202,"title":"","content":"I don't think LA by NIght forwards the idea that the Anarchs are the true protags to be honest. Nelli and Victor are basically Camarillia vamps that are only Anarchs for very specific reasons. The most sympathetic characters like Eva, Jasper and X are basically Autarkis that are forced to work with Anarchs against their will, Ib is true blue cam from ghoul to kindred. Also, I'd argue the most competent and likeable guest character is Fiorenza. If Vannevar hadn't been losing his shit LA would be in a very different place right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T17:11:17-07:00","id":1466209,"title":"","content":"Eh. They're all (barring Ib) under the Anarch moniker regardless to the point of Victor invoking Jeremy McNeil of all things at one point. The Camarilla gets basically obliterated from LA as a formal presence barring Ib and even her kinda sorta (considering she ends up questioning the validity of kindred existence itself, even if not in as hardcore a way as Eva does..). Beckett himself comes as if a voice from on high to refer to the Camarilla as an enemy the players will always have to be vigilant against in a &quot;see, even the signature npc everyone likes is saying...&quot;.<br /> <br /> The intent and context of the show felt pretty clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-01-2021, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T17:23:02-07:00","id":1466212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466202#post1466202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think LA by NIght forwards the idea that the Anarchs are the true protags to be honest. Nelli and Victor are basically Camarillia vamps that are only Anarchs for very specific reasons. The most sympathetic characters like Eva, Jasper and X are basically Autarkis that are forced to work with Anarchs against their will, Ib is true blue cam from ghoul to kindred. Also, I'd argue the most competent and likeable guest character is Fiorenza. If Vannevar hadn't been losing his shit LA would be in a very different place right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Anarchs have never been driven primarily by ideology. They're all committed to overthrowing the Camarilla in LA except for Ib and she's a zig-zag protagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T18:05:01-07:00","id":1466213,"title":"","content":"I think if the Cam had come with a decent offer half that coterie would have joined up. Jasper was considering it at one point and there really is no difference between Victor and someone like Eisenstadt. If Vannevar wasn't losing his mind and gave Victor a bit more respect than the other Barons showed him he would have flipped easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T18:10:02-07:00","id":1466214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466213#post1466213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if the Cam had come with a decent offer half that coterie would have joined up. Jasper was considering it at one point and there really is no difference between Victor and someone like Eisenstadt. If Vannevar wasn't losing his mind and gave Victor a bit more respect than the other Barons showed him he would have flipped easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that's all Anarchs. At the end of the day they're still vampires.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hell, Victor actually declared Praxis of LA at one point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.co