 that they are going in the Antagonist-Only bin. And even that book will be at least a few years down the track.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you have any particular insight about this? Or is it just assumed evil moustache-twirling by Paradox?<br /> <br /> It is unfortunately fair to say that a Fera Book would probably be some years in the future, considering we are still waiting for W5 core: however, if NWOD can be an indicator of the trajectory, in terms of how to frame some elements and adapt some rules (such as the Sabbat becoming an antagonist option like Belial's Brood, or the various mechanical adaptations and lore inspirations here and there), Fera shouldn't be off table, they had their own Forsaken supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T03:02:37-07:00","id":1466240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466239#post1466239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any particular insight about this? Or is it just assumed evil moustache-twirling by Paradox?<br /> <br /> It is unfortunately fair to say that a Fera Book would probably be some years in the future, considering we are still waiting for W5 core: however, if NWOD can be an indicator of the trajectory, in terms of how to frame some elements and adapt some rules (such as the Sabbat becoming an antagonist option like Belial's Brood, or the various mechanical adaptations and lore inspirations here and there), Fera shouldn't be off table, they had their own Forsaken supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things seem to be taking off with production finally. HUNTER: THE RECKONING is done and ready for release and no one expected that to be Game 2#.<br /> <br /> The Fera have also been mentioned in the stuff about WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE but we don't know what kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T03:37:22-07:00","id":1466243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466239#post1466239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do you have any particular insight about this? Or is it just assumed evil moustache-twirling by Paradox?<br /> <br /> It is unfortunately fair to say that a Fera Book would probably be some years in the future, considering we are still waiting for W5 core: however, if NWOD can be an indicator of the trajectory, in terms of how to frame some elements and adapt some rules (such as the Sabbat becoming an antagonist option like Belial's Brood, or the various mechanical adaptations and lore inspirations here and there), Fera shouldn't be off table, they had their own Forsaken supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No moustache twirling involved. Much like the Sabbat, The Fera form a significant proportion of currently running and supported campaigns and again like the Sabbat are often in an antagonistic role ( though, like the Sabbat, not always ).<br /> <br /> It seems that Paradox is intent on 'streamlining and focusing' as much as possible and Fera are an aspect of the game that will dilute that focus, so much like the Sabbat in that they fulfill a similar role in opposition to and occasional allies of convenience to the 'core splat' they are likely to be treated much the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T03:38:47-07:00","id":1466244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466243#post1466243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No moustache twirling involved. Much like the Sabbat, The Fera form a significant proportion of currently running and supported campaigns and again like the Sabbat are often in an antagonistic role ( though, like the Sabbat, not always ).<br /> <br /> It seems that Paradox is intent on 'streamlining and focusing' as much as possible and Fera are an aspect of the game that will dilute that focus, so much like the Sabbat in that they fulfill a similar role in opposition to and occasional allies of convenience to the 'core splat' they are likely to be treated much the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that comes very much from the view of the Sabbat as primarily a PC faction and less from the perspective that they were in the vast majority of games an antagonist faction. I don't think Fera have ever been people the Garou PCs were meant to kill.<br /> <br /> I think it's terrible the Sabbat don't have PC rules but the idea they were removed from such arbitrarily is silly. They were always the Black Spiral Dancers and Nephandi of the setting.<br /> <br /> (Why we needed rules for PCs of both factions, IMHO--Then again, I love Freak Legion)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T03:44:35-07:00","id":1466246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466237#post1466237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that's a weird comparison to make between the Sabbat and Fera.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I have the theory that Paradox was spooked by the previous controversies about the Ventrue who fed on children and Brujah Alt-RIght character. Basically, they did this because the fans had exploded with controversy toward &quot;evil&quot; vampires.<br /> <br /> No evidence to back this up.</div> </div> </div> </div>To my eye the Fera perform a similar role to the Sabbat in that they are generally cast in the role of antagonists against the ' core splat' who can be occasional strained allies in dire situations. I don't think Paradox is worried about controversy. Hell, Crusader Kings fanbase is a toxic cesspool of alt-right, bros and straight up nazis and Paradox doesn't care at all. <br /> <br /> I think its more about wanting to avoid ' dilution' of the core game experience, and Fera are fairly divorced from the core game experience.<br /> <br /> Hence why i think they'll be made antagonist only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T03:47:45-07:00","id":1466247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466244#post1466244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that comes very much from the view of the Sabbat as primarily a PC faction and less from the perspective that they were in the vast majority of games an antagonist faction. I don't think Fera have ever been people the Garou PCs were meant to kill.<br /> <br /> I think it's terrible the Sabbat don't have PC rules but the idea they were removed from such arbitrarily is silly. They were always the Black Spiral Dancers and Nephandi of the setting.<br /> <br /> (Why we needed rules for PCs of both factions, IMHO--Then again, I love Freak Legion)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean its hard not to see Sabbat as a PC faction when they have been for the past 29 years and made up fully 40-50% of the VtM games I've seen.<br /> <br /> I mean in the vast majority of Werewolf games Fera do play the part of antagonists in that they will be actively resisting Garou inroads into their territories, trying to get revenge for their fellows slaughtered by the Garou, defending their Kinfolk from Garou aggressors, stealing back stolen ancestral fetishes, forming alliances etc.<br /> <br /> No....the Baali and diabolists are the closest to BSDs of the VtM setting.<br /> <br /> 90% of the Garous problems are down to them killing people they weren't supposed to kill....its kinda their thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 11-02-2021, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T03:54:31-07:00","id":1466248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466247#post1466247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean its hard not to see Sabbat as a PC faction when they have been for the past 29 years and made up fully 40-50% of the VtM games I've seen.<br /> <br /> I mean in the vast majority of Werewolf games Fera do play the part of antagonists in that they will be actively resisting Garou inroads into their territories, trying to get revenge for their fellows slaughtered by the Garou, defending their Kinfolk from Garou aggressors, stealing back stolen ancestral fetishes, forming alliances etc.<br /> <br /> No....the Baali and diabolists are the closest to BSDs of the VtM setting.<br /> <br /> 90% of the Garous problems are down to them killing people they weren't supposed to kill....its kinda their thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummm, I've played Baali.<br /> <br /> The Baali have a Clan Book.<br /> <br /> They are absolutely a PC faction. Back then, though, they were willing to let you play EVIL PCs and unashamed about it. Pretending the Baali are more evil than the Sabbat is silly, though.<br /> <br /> The Fera, by contrast, have always been portrayed as people the Garou should be allied with and its a tragedy if they war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><