y divorced from the core game experience.<br /> <br /> Hence why i think they'll be made antagonist only.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IDK, I've seen and played a lot of Sabbat games, and I've also seen a lot of games where Sabbat was the main antagonist, while I've never seen a game where Fera were used, either as protagonists or antagonists (besides one multi-splat LARP with an Ananasi), but that could just be a matter of limited availability of material here in Italy.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, I don't really see Fera as antagonistic, they could just get a Player Option book and be done with it (something like a &quot;Cult of the Blood Gods&quot; detailing strange shapeshifting traditions and powers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T03:57:14-07:00","id":1466252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466250#post1466250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One is supported by the game line. The others should have been.<br /> <br /> But we'll find out about the Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, I give up again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T03:59:55-07:00","id":1466253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466251#post1466251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> IDK, I've seen and played a lot of Sabbat games, and I've also seen a lot of games where Sabbat was the main antagonist, while I've never seen a game where Fera were used, either as protagonists or antagonists (besides one multi-splat LARP with an Ananasi), but that could just be a matter of limited availability of material here in Italy.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, I don't really see Fera as antagonistic, they could just get a Player Option book and be done with it (something like a &quot;Cult of the Blood Gods&quot; detailing strange shapeshifting traditions and powers).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think probably 95% of my WtA campaigns over the last 30 years have involved Fera protagonists and/or antagonists, but the vast majority of the campaigns I've been involved in are set outside the US and Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date