erReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T21:42:05-07:00","id":1467016,"title":"","content":"So I mostly tend to ghost most of the time here but I have to ask how does this work exactly?<br /> <br /> To be specific Huitzilopoctli champion and patron of Mexico is a sun God as well as to a lesser extent Nergal is a sun God as well<br /> <br /> Why would this Shaitan a vampire choose to be worshiped as the God of the sun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 11-07-2021, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T00:18:36-07:00","id":1467019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467008#post1467008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure, but I don't see this version as being much beyond unashamed racism.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it the less sense it makes outside saying Mexico City is the backyard of the Devil and pre-Colombian cultures where actually demon-worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Baali are named for the Canaanite deity, who also allegedly had a taste for human sacrifice. The charitable implication being that Shaitan corrupts every culture he gets close to, be it Semitic or Mesoamerican. Ofc this also feeds into the 'the Bible is basically true, if inaccurate' trap I complained about, and negates personal responsibility for abhorrent cultural practices. <br /> <br /> The Ba'ali being more complicated than a B movie villains convention is also good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 11-07-2021, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T00:43:27-07:00","id":1467020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1466940#post1466940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You said Sabbat is like BSD/Nephandim. He said it's not and Baali are a more akin to BSD/Nephandi. How did you miss the disagreement? <br /> <br /> And &amp;quot;Baali are a PC faction because they have Clanbook&amp;quot; is silly. <br /> <br /> First of all Sabbat had two player's guides, their two main clans had 2 clanbooks each... yet we don't have playable Sabbat in V5.<br /> <br /> Secondly Clanbook: Baali has been created years ago by White Wolf for Vampire: the Dark Ages. I am not sure if V5 books even mention Baali (other than BJD) but do you really think Paradox would make them playable? <br /> <br /> Thirdly what we do at our own tables have no bearing on what Paradox wants to do with the franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, seriously, there is a 65-page thread just over there for arguing about the Sabbat and evil ParaWolf, can we try to discuss some other topics, including the one which started this discussion? It's a bit tiresome to see this argument pop up everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T00:56:25-07:00","id":1467021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467008#post1467008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure, but I don't see this version as being much beyond unashamed racism.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it the less sense it makes outside saying Mexico City is the backyard of the Devil and pre-Colombian cultures where actually demon-worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... Shaitan-as-Huitzilopochtli was probably done to tie jn the Aztec human sacrifices, in a incredibly crude and with racist overtones way. <br /> <br /> Also because it indirectly connects to a popular pseudo-historical theory which considers &quot;true&quot; Mesoamerican civilization as something started by Phoenicians or Egyptians. <br /> <br /> Speaking in general, population dynamics of the pre historical Americas would have made local Vampires more probably varistions of the KueJin coming through the Bering Straits, but considering how they were written, it would have been problematic as well. <br /> <br /> Curious to see if the will be using Drowned Legacies, they are mentioned heavily in nuCamarilla book and implied in Chicago and Cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T01:30:40-07:00","id":1467024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467021#post1467021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... Shaitan-as-Huitzilopochtli was probably done to tie jn the Aztec human sacrifices, in a incredibly crude and with racist overtones way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to make it clear to anyone who can't care to look it in other places:<br /> <br /> Huitzilopochtli isn't particularly linked to human sacrifices. Human sacrifices were a generalized practice in Mesoamerican cultures, although not in the ridiculous proportions of Spanish reports.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T02:40:18-08:00","id":1467033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467024#post1467024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to make it clear to anyone who can't care to look it in other places:<br /> <br /> Huitzilopochtli isn't particularly linked to human sacrifices. Human sacrifices were a generalized practice in Mesoamerican cultures, although not in the ridiculous proportions of Spanish reports.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but those were also the epic times when Amsterdam was considered in &quot;A World of Darkness&quot; a Scandinavian city, so ... i'm not surprised of this less than accurate depiction \ud83d\ude05","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T03:16:37-08:00","id":1467036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That rings a bit hollow given the drastic alterations already present in the 5e universe. And plenty of people have said changes to sects or some clans and bloodlines already makes them not feel like them. I'm not clamoring for them to make KotE in 5e because I don't think they would have done a good job but that doesn't really feel like a point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having thought about it some more I fully agree with you. Point retracted. They've changed so much already &quot;cough Sabbat incoherent mess in V5 cough&quot; that using it as an excuse for not including the Wan Kuei makes no sense whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T04:33:52-08:00","id":1467039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467016#post1467016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I mostly tend to ghost most of the time here but I have to ask how does this work exactly?<br /> <br /> To be specific Huitzilopoctli champion and patron of Mexico is a sun God as well as to a lesser extent Nergal is a sun God as well<br /> <br /> Why would this Shaitan a vampire choose to be worshiped as the God of the sun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason as Mithras.<br /> <br /> Vampires love choosing popular deities as their divine identities. There was a funny bit in the original FOLLOWERS OF SET CLANBOOK where a FOS took a role as a god of the dead and was irritated he was less popular than a goddess of joy that his childe took.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T05:36:49-08:00","id":1467044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467021#post1467021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... Shaitan-as-Huitzilopochtli was probably done to tie jn the Aztec human sacrifices, in a incredibly crude and with racist overtones way. <br /> <br /> Also because it indirectly connects to a popular pseudo-historical theory which considers &amp;quot;true&amp;quot; Mesoamerican civilization as something started by Phoenicians or Egyptians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that when it was released in 1993 we were still rocking on the newly released Windows 3.1, the Internet was still dial-up with AOL and Netscape were the primary means of accessing it and the beta iteration of the pdf had just been shown off at a conference. Cell phones and their plans were so expensive and limited (a few hours was a huge deal) that their extensive use by Mulder and Scully on The X-Files was mocked as breaking the FBI\u2019s budget.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do research back then, you pretty much had to rely on whatever physical books were in your local library. So I\u2019d be far less likely to impute motives like racism to what is more likely just what sources were available in libraries of the American Midwest c. 1990.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T05:49:49-08:00","id":1467045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467044#post1467044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider that when it was released in 1993 we were still rocking on the newly released Windows 3.1, the Internet was still dial-up with AOL and Netscape were the primary means of accessing it and the beta iteration of the pdf had just been shown off at a conference. Cell phones and their plans were so expensive and limited (a few hours was a huge deal) that their extensive use by Mulder and Scully on The X-Files was mocked as breaking the FBI\u2019s budget.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do research back then, you pretty much had to rely on whatever physical books were in your local library. So I\u2019d be far less likely to impute motives like racism to what is more likely just what sources were available in libraries of the American Midwest c. 1990.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying that traditional deities are stand-ins for demons is &quot;problematic&quot; isn't necessarily something that is overreaching the mark. Even if you, quite justifiably, consider human sacrifices to be a horrifying waste of life and morally repugnant from your ethical system, it is something that noteworthy that they went the extra mile here with. Its not <b>just</b> that Huitzilopochtli is a Kindred impersonating (or even inspiring) an Aztec god.<br /> <br /> It's that he's also a demon-worshipping embodiment of absolute evil that is worse than the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> But I think we're way way off LA by Night and arguably even worse than the Sabbat: The Black Hand thread. We can make a new thread about the subject if anyone wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T08:13:35-08:00","id":1467050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467044#post1467044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider that when it was released in 1993 we were still rocking on the newly released Windows 3.1, the Internet was still dial-up with AOL and Netscape were the primary means of accessing it and the beta iteration of the pdf had just been shown off at a conference. Cell phones and their plans were so expensive and limited (a few hours was a huge deal) that their extensive use by Mulder and Scully on The X-Files was mocked as breaking the FBI\u2019s budget.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do research back then, you pretty much had to rely on whatever physical books were in your local library. So I\u2019d be far less likely to impute motives like racism to what is more likely just what sources were available in libraries of the American Midwest c. 1990.</div> </div> </div> </div>I surely wouldn't ascribe racist thoughts to original White Wolf authors: the World of Darkness has always an unashamedly progressive franchise, giving voice and representation to minorities and the marginals in Western society.<br /> <br /> It's just these things were written in a time where, as you rightly underline, possibilities of research were limited, by young authors, and with very different sensibilities from nowadays. I don't particularly blame them of anything for having written it like this back in 1993: today, such a plot would be written differently, and rightly so.<br /> <br /> (Still, placing Amsterdam on the map should have been easy!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T09:07:20-08:00","id":1467052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467044#post1467044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider that when it was released in 1993 we were still rocking on the newly released Windows 3.1, the Internet was still dial-up with AOL and Netscape were the primary means of accessing it and the beta iteration of the pdf had just been shown off at a conference. Cell phones and their plans were so expensive and limited (a few hours was a huge deal) that their extensive use by Mulder and Scully on The X-Files was mocked as breaking the FBI\u2019s budget.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do research back then, you pretty much had to rely on whatever physical books were in your local library. So I\u2019d be far less likely to impute motives like racism to what is more likely just what sources were available in libraries of the American Midwest c. 1990.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse than that, as Netscape was <i>founded</i> in 1994 and AOL would reach the first spot as main provider for the US in 1995 (with staggering 3 million users). Cell phones don't even matter as at the time they didn't access the internet, they are telephones.<br /> <br /> Yet none of this matter. Using foreign gods and cultures as <b><i>The Work of the Devil\u2122</i></b> is racism. Racism being widespread back then doesn't make it less racist. The peoples and religions affected pretty much existed at the time and went completely ignored in favor of standard WASP view.<br /> <br /> This is the kind of attitude that gives Christians a bad name outside their own circles, being utterly offended when your god isn't treated as the First Cause, an extremely specific, advanced and debatable theological concept, but saying that treating other religions and cultures as the work of your devil is acceptable or at least comprehensible because they didn't have good internet.<br /> <br /> By the way, they had access to academic libraries, not to any street stand where no one knew the difference between archaeology and Indiana Jones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467045#post1467045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think we're way way off LA by Night and arguably even worse than the Sabbat: The Black Hand thread. We can make a new thread about the subject if anyone wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the same, but It isn't completely off mark as more than a <b>third</b> of LA County population is of Mexican descent alone.<br /> <br /> So it is weirdly fitting even if tangential, as this kind of consideration does affect a sizable portion of the city, bigger than the &quot;white&quot; population. &quot;White&quot; because while in the US Latinos aren't considered white, in Latin America we have a somewhat different concept of what constitutes a white person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467050#post1467050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I surely wouldn't ascribe racist thoughts to original White Wolf authors: the World of Darkness has always an unashamedly progressive franchise, giving voice and representation to minorities and the marginals in Western society.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but the definition of racism isn't about consciously choosing to be a bigot. Actually racist attitudes are rarely if ever conscious.<br /> <br /> Early WW did put a lot of effort in being open to diversity. Yet, there were some glaring flaws, and the origin of those flaws is racism, as one of its effects is to make people assume the popular concept of another group is correct without trying to confirm with said group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T09:10:40-08:00","id":1467054,"title":"","content":"Similarly related, Fiorenza the Ventrue is basically the Signature character of 5th Edition and her primary accomplishment for the Camarilla is the retaking of Mexico City. She ends LA by Night by inviting Victor and Ib to take refuge in the city if Los Angeles has become too hot for them. I think that one of the bigger failings of V5 has been the lack of signature characters and LA By Night went a long way to giving us a sense of how it was meant to be played.<br /> <br /> I really want them to make a city sourcebook or Chronicle for this game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T09:49:26-08:00","id":1467061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467054#post1467054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want them to make a city sourcebook or Chronicle for this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a worthy endeavor, as some people aren't so keen on watching actual game play, and it is hard to use as source anyway. By the content here, it seems it was really good at showcasing the edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T14:55:02-08:00","id":1467382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod#post1465967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, LA by Night is over and I have to say it did a lot better at ending in a &quot;suitable&quot; V:TM way than I expected to. One of the complaints about the series has been that it was a little too Light and Soft for what is a horror game. Personally, I don't think that there's a &quot;wrong&quot; way to play V:TM but I did think they could have gone darker.<br /> <br /> Well, I'm glad they did.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Chacun \u00e0 son go\u00fbt. Personally I found the lack of a &quot;it's cool to be evil&quot; vibe - first in Dawkins' cerebral in-character videos as Lord Camden, then in LAbN - a major selling point for V5. I'm aware that many prefer a darker, more Sabbat-adjacent tone, and LAbN may not have been for them, but to me, the core book spoiled some wonderful material by dropping heavy hints that if you weren't playing a particularly nihilistic type of Scandi-Noir, you were Doing It Wrong. I came out of LAbN liking V5 better than I did before. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T18:53:11-08:00","id":1467401,"title":"","content":"Look, if you are not running a game where everything is so drowning in crushing despair that it makes anhedonia look good by comparison, then you not not doing VtM right!<br /> <br /> (cough)<br /> <br /> Joking aside, I am not one to shame people for doing their games &quot;right.&quot; But as a matter of personal taste, LAbN could have used more &quot;personal horror&quot; and less silly melodrama. But in any case,the series helped promote RPGs in general and VtM in particular, so kudos to everyone involved.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T19:22:25-08:00","id":1467403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467401#post1467401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, if you are not running a game where everything is so drowning in crushing despair that it makes anhedonia look good by comparison, then you not not doing VtM right!<br /> <br /> (cough)<br /> <br /> Joking aside, I am not one to shame people for doing their games &quot;right.&quot; But as a matter of personal taste, LAbN could have used more &quot;personal horror&quot; and less silly melodrama. But in any case,the series helped promote RPGs in general and VtM in particular, so kudos to everyone involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I was surprised by the ending where the fellowship broke up and a lot of the characters turned against one another with some dead or entering permanent torpor.<br /> <br /> It was a surprisingly bold storytelling choice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T02:44:23-08:00","id":1467423,"title":"","content":"I personally have nothing against happy endings and my games use them with some frequency, but this is not a requirement. The approach of VtM as a world where nothing can be good is not only depressing but outright boring for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T17:38:53-08:00","id":1467619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465967-spoilers-la-by-night-ending-a-k-a-the-state-of-la-in-the-wod?p=1467403#post1467403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I said, I was surprised by the ending where the fellowship broke up and a lot of the characters turned against one another with some dead or entering permanent torpor.<br /> <br /> It was a surprisingly bold storytelling choice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It felt a little out of left field for a few of them (I would've liked to see the divide between Nelli and Victor develop). But at the same time it accurately reflects the corrupting nature of Caine's curse. In-time all bonds will fade as personal power and survival take precedence, it's not surprising that the two Baron's in particular come into conflict.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the ending was bitter-sweet, which I think is appropriate for a VTM chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}